{"ts": 0.034556, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97mMODULE — env: variables and the prompt\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nFive short lessons, then a gate. This module stands alone and saves\r\nnothing. Type \u001b[92mquit\u001b[0m to leave at any point.\r\n\r\nYou will see:\r\n  variables, and how the shell uses them\r\n  \u001b[92mexport\u001b[0m, and what a child program receives\r\n", "len": 289}
{"ts": 0.034641, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "  \u001b[92mPATH\u001b[0m, the list the shell searches for programs\r\n  the prompt, which is a variable too\r\n  where these settings live for real\r\n\r\nEverything stays inside this tutor's practice shell. Your own\r\nconfiguration files are not touched.\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Type \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m to begin lesson 1.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 296}
{"ts": 0.037732, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;90mnext\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(go on)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mshow\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(this screen again)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mprev\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(back)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mquit\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(save and leave)\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 159}
{"ts": 0.038006, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 251}
