{"ts": 0.086515, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m──\u001b[0m \u001b[90mModule · env\u001b[0m \u001b[90m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m \u001b[93m2 of 5\u001b[0m \u001b[90m──\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 244}
{"ts": 0.086546, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\r\n", "len": 2}
{"ts": 0.089959, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97menv 2 — export and child programs\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nA program the shell starts is a \u001b[36mchild\u001b[0m. It receives only the\r\nvariables that were \u001b[36mexported\u001b[0m. Single quotes stop this shell from\r\nreplacing \u001b[92m$pet\u001b[0m, so the child does it.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[92mpet=owl\u001b[0m                          \u001b[90m# set it again: new screen, new shell\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mbash -c 'echo [$pet]'\u001b[0m            \u001b[90m# prints [] : the child sees nothing\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mexport pet\u001b[0m                       \u001b[90m# mark it for children\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mbash -c 'echo [$pet]'\u001b[0m            \u001b[90m# prints [owl]\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92menv | grep '^pet='\u001b[0m               \u001b[90m# now it is listed\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 647}
{"ts": 0.090046, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\r\nNotice that \u001b[92mexport\u001b[0m copies nothing. It marks the name so every\r\nchild gets the value at the moment it starts.\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Run the five lines in order, then type \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 194}
{"ts": 0.093129, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;90mnext\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(go on)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mshow\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(this screen again)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mprev\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(back)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mquit\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(save and leave)\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 159}
{"ts": 0.093412, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 253}
