{"ts": 0.113043, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m──\u001b[0m \u001b[90mModule · env\u001b[0m \u001b[90m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m \u001b[93m3 of 5\u001b[0m \u001b[90m──\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 244}
{"ts": 0.113069, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\r\n", "len": 2}
{"ts": 0.116268, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97menv 3 — PATH is a list\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[92mPATH\u001b[0m is a variable that holds folders separated by \u001b[92m:\u001b[0m. When you\r\ntype a command name, the shell looks in those folders, in order, and\r\nruns the first match.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[92mecho \"$PATH\"\u001b[0m                  \u001b[90m# one long line\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mecho \"$PATH\" | tr : '\\n'\u001b[0m      \u001b[90m# one folder per line\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 356}
{"ts": 0.116332, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "  \u001b[92mcommand -v ls\u001b[0m                 \u001b[90m# the folder where ls was found\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nThis is why \u001b[92mcommand -v\u001b[0m (Stage 4) could answer: it reads this list.\r\nA program in a folder that is not on the list is not found by name.\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Run the three lines, then type \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 296}
{"ts": 0.119513, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;90mnext\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(go on)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mshow\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(this screen again)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mprev\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(back)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mquit\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(save and leave)\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 159}
