{"ts": 0.143471, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97menv 4 — the prompt is a variable\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nThe text before your cursor is the variable \u001b[92mPS1\u001b[0m. Change it and the\r\nprompt changes at once.\r\n\r\n", "len": 153}
{"ts": 0.14353, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "  \u001b[92mPS1='me> '\u001b[0m       \u001b[90m# the prompt is now me>\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mPS1='$ '\u001b[0m         \u001b[90m# and now a plain dollar sign\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nTry both. Then type \u001b[92mnext\u001b[0m and look at the prompt on the next screen.\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Change the prompt, then type \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 273}
{"ts": 0.146592, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;90mnext\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(go on)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mshow\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(this screen again)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mprev\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(back)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mquit\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(save and leave)\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 159}
