{"ts": 0.167725, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m──\u001b[0m \u001b[90mModule · env\u001b[0m \u001b[90m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m \u001b[93m5 of 5\u001b[0m \u001b[90m──\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 244}
{"ts": 0.16777, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\r\n", "len": 2}
{"ts": 0.1707, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97menv 5 — where this lives for real\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nYour prompt went back: each screen starts a fresh shell, and the tutor\r\nignores your own configuration files so every learner sees the same thing.\r\nA real terminal reads one file when it starts:\r\n  \u001b[94m~/.bashrc\u001b[0m   if your login shell is bash\r\n", "len": 298}
{"ts": 0.17076, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "  \u001b[94m~/.zshrc\u001b[0m    if it is zsh \u001b[90m(check: echo $SHELL)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90mmacOS with bash reads ~/.bash_profile instead.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nLines you could add there:\r\n  \u001b[92mPS1='$ '\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mexport PATH=\"$HOME/bin:$PATH\"\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[91mQuit the tutor\u001b[0m, open a new terminal, edit the file there. The tutor\r\nwill not touch it. Open another new terminal to see the change.\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Read the lines, then type \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m to take the gate.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 437}
{"ts": 0.174036, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;90mnext\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(go on)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mshow\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(this screen again)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mprev\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(back)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mquit\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(save and leave)\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 159}
